---
import { CAREER } from "../data";
---

<section class="px-6 py-24 lg:py-32">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
    <div class="text-center">
      <h2
        class="font-heading text-3xl font-bold uppercase leading-tight tracking-tight md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl"
      >
        Built by someone who&apos;s been<br /> on your side of the table
      </h2>
      <p
        class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ship-gray-400"
      >
        SHIP comes from years leading engineering in the most regulated,
        highest-stakes corners of finance — market making, derivatives risk,
        brokerage and trading platforms across multiple asset classes and
        jurisdictions. The problem it solves was learned at that scale: how
        quietly real work drifts from intent once the stakes and the headcount
        get large.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-6">
      <div class="space-y-3">
        {
          CAREER.map((c) => (
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 rounded-lg border border-ship-gray-800 bg-ship-gray-900/30 px-5 py-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:gap-4">
              <a
                href={c.url}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="shrink-0 font-heading text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-ship-accent transition-colors hover:text-ship-accent-hover hover:underline"
              >
                {c.company}
              </a>
              <span class="text-sm text-ship-gray-400">{c.role}</span>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>

    <blockquote
      class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-2xl border-l-2 border-ship-accent/40 pl-6 text-base italic leading-relaxed text-ship-gray-300"
    >
      &ldquo;At scale-up after scale-up I watched leaders run on narrative —
      standups, decks, green dashboards — while the artefact trail told a
      different story. The painful part was never typing code faster; it was
      discovering three weeks before a release that we were building the wrong
      thing. SHIP exists to collapse that gap: goals at the top, evidence from
      Git and Jira and docs below, drift in the open before it is
      expensive.&rdquo;
    </blockquote>
  </div>
</section>
